-- title:
--   A Frobenius–Verschiebung identity for φ^∨ on the special fibre
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, a commutative ring $O$ with an $O$-algebra structure on $\mathbb{Z}/p$, and a $p$-divisible group $\mathcal{G}$ over $O$ of height $h$: a family of finite free cocommutative $O$-Hopf algebras $\mathcal{G}.\mathrm{level}\,v$ with surjective bialgebra transitions, $\operatorname{finrank}_O \mathcal{G}.\mathrm{level}\,v = p^{vh}$, and $\ker(\mathcal{G}.\mathrm{transition}\,v)$ equal to the image of the augmentation ideal ($=\ker$ of the counit) under the $p^v$-fold convolution power of the identity. Given a family $\varphi$ of bialgebra endomorphisms and a family $D_p$ of bialgebra automorphisms of the levels, both commuting with the transitions, the hypotheses provide three further towers over $\mathbb{Z}/p$ of the same shape (finite free cocommutative Hopf algebras, surjective transitions, ranks $p^{v h_T}$, $p^{v h_B}$, $p^{v h_1}$, $p^{v h_2}$, kernels the corresponding torsion ideals): a quotient tower $T$ of $\mathbb{Z}/p\otimes_O\mathcal{G}.\mathrm{level}\,v$ via compatible surjections $\pi_T$, a tower $B$ embedded compatibly by $j_B$ with $\ker \pi_T$ the ideal generated by $j_B$ of the augmentation ideal of $B$, and inside $B$ an exact pair $G_2 \hookrightarrow B \twoheadrightarrow G_1$ (compatible $j_2$, $\pi_1$, with $\ker\pi_1$ the ideal generated by $j_2$ of the augmentation ideal of $G_2$). It is assumed that $T$ carries automorphisms $\mathrm{Ver}_T$ whose Cartier dual map is $\psi\mapsto\psi^p$, that $\varphi$ and $D_p$ descend to $T$ and restrict along $j_B$ to $\varphi_B$, $D_B$, that $\varphi_B$, $D_B$ induce $\varphi_1$ on $G_1$ and $\varphi_2$, $d_2$ on $G_2$, that $G_1$ carries $\mathrm{Ver}_1$ with Cartier dual map $\psi\mapsto\psi^p$, and finally that $\varphi_1 = \mathrm{Ver}_1$ and $\varphi_2 x = d_2(x^p)$ at every level. The conclusion, at level $1$: for every bialgebra endomorphism $F_k$ of $\mathbb{Z}/p\otimes_O\mathcal{G}.\mathrm{level}\,1$ with $F_k x = x^p$, and every $\mathbb{Z}/p$-algebra endomorphism $F_D$ of its Cartier dual $\operatorname{Hom}_{\mathbb{Z}/p}(\mathbb{Z}/p\otimes_O\mathcal{G}.\mathrm{level}\,1,\mathbb{Z}/p)$ with $F_D\psi = \psi^p$, there are $n\in\mathbb{N}$ and bialgebra endomorphisms $a$, $b$ of the Cartier dual such that the $n$-th composition power of $\mathrm{CartierDual.map}(1\otimes\varphi_1)$ equals the convolution product of $F_D\circ a$ and $b\circ \mathrm{CartierDual.map}\,F_k$ as linear endomorphisms. Note that only the existence of some exponent $n$ is asserted, not the value $n = 2$.
--
--   This is the Eichler–Shimura-type $(F,V)$-relation for the dual of an endomorphism of a $p$-divisible group whose special fibre is an extension of a group with a Verschiebung-type quotient filtration by a multiplicative part, in the style of the arguments of Mazur–Wiles and Wiles on ordinary $\lambda$-adic representations. It feeds the corresponding statement for the reduction of the Hecke operator $U_p$ acting on the $p$-divisible group of the Néron model of $J_H$ at $p$, used in establishing the required local behaviour of the associated Galois representations.
-- source:
